    "https://careers.alaska.edu/university-of-alaska-system-office": {
      "title": "Explore the University of Alaska System Office",
      "description": "University of Alaska System Office Skip to main content UA Careers Benefits Search Jobs All Jobs Staff Jobs Faculty Jobs Temporary Jobs Temporary Faculty Jobs Student Jobs Internal Jobs Universities UA Anchorage UA Fairbanks UA Southeast UA System Office Internal Jobs My Profile Kiosk mode Explore the University of Alaska System Office UA System Office Staff UA System Office Student UA System Office Temp Staff UA Internal Jobs Search all University of Alaska jobs Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me Mission Statement for the System Office Through its support of the Board of Regents, the three universities with distinct missions, and their community campuses, the University of Alaska System Office advances higher education and honors the Indigenous and diverse peoples of Alaska. The University of Alaska System Office manages corporate responsibilities, strategically stewards shared resources, and works with the universities to implement Regents' policies and directions to align with current and future needs of the state. Learn more about the System Office Mission Statement . About the University of Alaska System The University of Alaska inspires learning, and advances and disseminates knowledge through teaching, research, and public service, emphasizing the North and its peoples. The University of Alaska is a land-, sea- and space-grant system of higher education established in 1917. The UA system’s three universities (UAA, UAF and UAS) are separately accredited institutions with 13 community campuses and extended learning centers across the state of Alaska. All three universities deliver extensive e-Learning instruction anywhere students are located. Our three universities, along with their associated community campuses, are an integral part of our state and the communities they serve. The UA system provides 90%  of Alaska's post-secondary education. Study areas include short-course workforce training, associate degrees, bachelor’s and master’s degrees, as well as doctorates. Explore the many programs and degrees that we offer on our campuses or via e-Learning. Military Resources Financial Aid Transfer Information Academic Programs Register your interest today! Enter your First Name (required) 0c3c7607 Enter your Last Name (required) e5696061 Enter your Email Address (required) c522f668 I want to learn more about the following areas of interest (required) adb82839 Research Skilled Trades Financial/Accounting Marketing/Communications Student Services Information Technology Administration/Office Human Resources Register your interest! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Register for job alerts! Use the form below to register for job alerts.  We send out job alerts when new opportunities are posted that match the criteria you selected. Enter your First Name (required) acc5fa60 Enter your Last Name (required) b2977305 Enter your Email Address (required) cf3e4397 Select the type of job alerts you want to receive 01293bed Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Employment Type Locations Register for Job Alerts! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Frequently Asked Questions How do I apply for a job at UA? Click our 'Search Jobs' button at the top to find your perfect role! Click 'Apply Now'! Fill out the form! Sit back & relax and we'll be in touch soon! How do I find out what jobs are available at the University of Alaska? All job postings within the University of Alaska are available 24 hours a day on our careers website . These positions are located at the three main UA Campuses, Anchorage, Fairbanks, and Juneau, as well as all the rural campus within the state. What is it like living in Alaska? We have an entire page dedicated to what life in Alaska is like. Please visit the Living in Alaska website to view some of the wonderful information we have put together for you. What benefits do you offer? Visit the UA HR Benefits website to learn more about UA's comprehensive benefit packages. The University of Alaska (alaska.edu/alaska) is an Equal Opportunity/Equal Access Employer and Educational Institution. The University is committed to a policy of non-discrimination (alaska.edu/nondiscrimination) against individuals on the basis of any legally protected status. This site is maintained by UA Office of Information Technology. For questions or concerns, please contact the OIT Support Center. For questions or comments regarding this page, contact helpdesk@alaska.edu | ⓒ UA Privacy Policy Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalise content such as job recommendations, and to analyse our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device I do not accept I accept Please choose the location(s)"
